WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:03.540
- Home security cameras.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.850
They can be great for
monitoring deliveries,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:06.840
keeping an eye on your house.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.360
And of course, spying on your cats.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.450
In fact, around 14% of US
households with broadband

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.520
now use an internet connected camera,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.380
and the US market for
home security cameras

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.320
is projected to continue
growing rapidly through 2030.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.720
But their popularity has come at a cost.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.390
- Amazon's ring doorbell may
not be as private as you think.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.480
- [Newscaster] Hackers tapping
into those home cameras.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.280
- [Hacker] I'll leave
you and your family alone

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.231
or I could do this.

00:00:30.231 --> 00:00:31.320
(alarm blaring)

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.210
- Just this year, Amazon-owned ring

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.880
handed over surveillance
footage to law enforcement

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.600
11 times without a warrant
or customer consent.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.820
- The company said the
request met its exception

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.940
for emergencies, which it
defines as danger of death

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.950
or serious physical injury.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.510
And since cats have nine lives

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.530
and always land on their feet,

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.560
I figured Koneko, a
Manhattan-based cat cafe

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.840
wouldn't it be at any risk of
law enforcement stepping in.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.210
But there's a stereotype with cats

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.410
and it's that they're burglars.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.860
And we'd like to prove
otherwise with this video.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.150
So, that's why it's the perfect place

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.670
to come and outline some dos
and don'ts for you to consider

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.050
when setting up and installing

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.350
some of the latest smart
surveillance cameras.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.110
Of course, Joe Golka,
Koneko's cattery guide

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.480
was with us all day to
ensure that these rescued

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.730
and adoptable cats were
happy and comfortable.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:18.630
- Right?

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.740
You're gonna hang with me?

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.195
- [Kenny] And that no real paws were used.

00:01:22.195 --> 00:01:23.028
- [Nicole] Is my hand in it.

00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:23.861
- [Staff] Yeah.

00:01:23.861 --> 00:01:25.470
- [Kenny] If you want
your valuable recordings

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.940
shielded from prying eyes

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.670
you should try to enable
end-to-end encryption.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.610
But what does that mean
and what does it do?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.280
To keep it simple, let's
say cameras typically use

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.960
one of two encryption types.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.250
There's standard encryption

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.470
and then there's end-to-end encryption.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.740
Imagine two companies,
Cat Cam and Dog Cam.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.586
Cat-Cam has end-to-end encryption
which means the only user

00:01:46.586 --> 00:01:49.530
with the key to decrypt
your video files is you.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.780
Well, you and anyone you
share the account with.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.660
So, end-to-end encryption
protects your data from hackers

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.700
and prevents it from
being viewed by others

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.190
such as law enforcement or Cat Cam.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.390
Dog Cam encrypts your video

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.700
when it's traveling from
you to company servers,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.650
but it doesn't do it end-to-end,

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.020
which means the company
can also hold the key

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.970
to decrypt your recordings.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.500
If you're looking for
end-to-end encryption,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.940
Nicole recommends a camera that works

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.090
with Apple's Smart Home
platform called HomeKit.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.670
- I like these devices
because end-to-end encryption

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.170
is on by default.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.040
Logitech's circle view camera
or doorbell are good picks.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.070
They work indoor or outdoor
and have face recognition

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.290
to identify different
people in your household

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.880
or frequent visitors.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.320
- [Kenny] End-to-end
encryption isn't limited

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.880
to just HomeKit cameras.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.330
For instance, you can now
enable it on some ring cameras.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.790
But it's not on by default
and another important note,

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.010
it's not available for
their battery powered models

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.950
and disables some key features.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.300
No matter which brand you choose,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.700
be sure to use a secure password.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.190
Don't point your camera at private spaces.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.800
Security cameras usually
have ultra wide lenses

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.000
that capture far more

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.580
than say a normal smartphone camera would.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.310
So it's important to consider
the expectation of privacy

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.540
when installing one.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.650
Ask yourself.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.210
What would you be comfortable with?

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.310
If you've got a doorbell-style
security camera,

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.490
try not to capture a shot into
your neighbor's front window.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.500
And if there's a zone in
your camera's field of view

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.820
you'd rather not capture,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.640
try enabling motion
detection or privacy zones.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.500
- Cameras from these brands all feature

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.090
activity zone triggering.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.990
Any HomeKit camera, such as
those from Eve or Logitech,

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.510
Ring, Google Nest and Arlo.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.180
Ring devices can also
set up privacy zones,

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.290
which will black out areas
from being recorded in videos.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.810
- [Kenny] Do consider location factors.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.330
If you're looking to monitor
an entire space indoors

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.120
it's best to keep your
camera at a higher location.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.010
This will give you the
widest field of view.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:41.917
Then ask yourself,

00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:44.640
"Do I need night vision
in my camera's location?"

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.890
If so, make sure your security camera

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.410
has an infrared spotlight
which will enable it

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.680
to capture video and images
in little to no light.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.470
Also, if your camera is
being used as a baby monitor

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.570
or in a location where
silence is important,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.270
it's worth noting many
security cameras can click

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.980
when activating their infrared light.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.690
- If you're in a noise
sensitive environment

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.280
try disabling night vision

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.100
and buying a separate
infrared illuminator.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.671
And always be sure to let
everyone in your household

00:04:10.671 --> 00:04:13.290
or location know there's a camera.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:16.500
- [Kenny] Don't forget
about hardware quirks.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.820
In the world of security cameras

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.280
you have outdoor cameras
and indoor cameras.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.410
Battery powdered cameras
can live outside for months

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.850
without having to be recharged

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.130
or having any pesky wires run to them

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.130
which makes it easy to forget
when they need to be charged.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.440
Don't be a jerk or creep.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.570
- [Nicole] Many brands
let you clip recordings

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.330
which can then be posted to social media.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.750
Ring even has its own
network called Neighbors.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.060
- This for a place like
Koneko can be great

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.970
when they wanna post clips
of their in-house influencers

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.250
for public consumption.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.530
But security cam users
should always think twice

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.300
before posting to social media.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.210
That's because it's easy for
nefarious internet passersby

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.930
to triangulate your location
simply by landmarks outside.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.900
Also a case of mistaken
identity or misunderstanding

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.750
can lead to an accidental
tragedy, somebody getting fired,

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:04.800
all sorts of bad things.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.320
So, before you post something
online, take a breath,

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.683
think twice and consider the outcome.

00:05:13.096 --> 00:05:16.982
(staff member laughing softly)

